    26	
    27	## bot_flags.csv.gz
    28	One row per flag raised by the platform's bot screening (`docs/BOT_SCREENING.md`). A user can have rows of both rules,
    29	and more than one row of the same rule.
    30	
    31	| Column | Meaning |
    32	|---|---|
    33	| `user_id` | the flagged user |
    34	| `rule` | the screening rule that raised the flag: `ua_crawler` or `velocity` |
    35	| `flagged_at` | when the flag was raised (for each rule: `docs/BOT_SCREENING.md`) |
    36	
    37	## pageviews.csv.gz
    38	One row per product pageview, logged when the page has loaded. The assignment service assigns a user when the page
    39	is requested, so the pageview on which a user was assigned has no row if the user left before the page loaded: an
    40	assigned user need not have a pageview at `assigned_at`, and can have no pageview row at all.
    41	
    42	| Column | Meaning |
    43	|---|---|
    44	| `pageview_id` | the pageview (text); unique per row |
    45	| `user_id` | the user |
    46	| `ts` | when the page loaded |
    47	| `clicked` | 1 if at least one module_click event was logged on this pageview, else 0 (precomputed for dashboards) |
    48	
    49	## module_clicks.csv.gz
    50	One row per module_click event of the related-items module (`docs/TRACKING.md`). Times are to the second, so two
    51	clicks on the same element in the same second give two identical rows; each row is one event.
    52	
    53	| Column | Meaning |
    54	|---|---|
    55	| `pageview_id` | the pageview the event was logged on (`pageviews.csv.gz`); the event belongs to that pageview's user |
    56	| `user_id` | the user |
    57	| `ts` | when the click happened; at or after the pageview's `ts` |
    58	| `target` | the `data-target` value of the clicked element (`docs/TRACKING.md`) |
===== docs/TRACKING.md =====
     1	# Tracking: the related-items module
     2	
     3	Data platform documentation. It applies to every experiment export of this layout.
     4	
     5	## module_click events
     6	The related-items module on product pages logs one `module_click` event per click on any clickable element inside the
     7	module. Each event records the pageview it happened on, the user, the time of the click and the clicked element's
     8	`data-target` value. Exports hold these events in `module_clicks.csv.gz`, and `pageviews.clicked` is derived from
     9	them (`docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md`).
    10	
    11	| `data-target` | Element | What a click on it does |
    12	|---|---|---|
    13	| `item:<product_id>` | a product card | opens that product's page |
    14	| `nav:prev`, `nav:next` | the previous and next arrows of the v2 carousel | scroll the carousel; open nothing |
    15	| `link:all` | the "See all" link, in every module version from 2026-09-08 | opens the list page of all related items |
    16	
    17	## Module versions
    18	| Version | What the module shows |
    19	|---|---|
    20	| v1 | the current module: a row of six product cards |
    21	| v2 | related items v2 (RI-311): a carousel of 12 product cards with previous and next arrows |
    22	
    23	Other experiments test other layouts or rankings of the cards; v2 is the only version with arrows. Since 2026-09-08
    24	every version also shows the "See all" link.
    25	
    26	The module version is set per experiment arm: from a user's assignment on, every product pageview of the user shows
    27	the version of the user's arm, as the experiment's launch record sets it (EXP-2291: v1 in A, v2 in B). Before the
    28	assignment, every user sees v1.
    29	
    30	## Changelog
    31	- 2025-04-14: `module_click` events logged for every clickable element of the module.
    32	- 2026-09-01: v2 available to experiments, per arm (EXP-2291 shows it in arm B).
    33	- 2026-09-08: "See all" link (`link:all`) added to every module version (RI-318).
===== docs/BOT_SCREENING.md =====
     1	# Bot screening
     2	
     3	Data platform documentation. It applies to every experiment export of this layout.
     4	
     5	The platform screens traffic for bots with two rules. Every flag is one row of `bot_flags.csv.gz` (`user_id`, `rule`,
     6	`flagged_at`). A user can be flagged by both rules.
     7	
     8	| Rule | In use since | What it looks at | When it runs | `flagged_at` |
     9	|---|---|---|---|---|
    10	| `ua_crawler` | 2024-03 | the client: a crawler user agent, or an IP address in a data-centre range | on the client's first request to the platform (any page; it need not be a product pageview of the export) | the time of that first request; one row per flagged user |
    11	| `velocity` | 2026-08-28 (SEC-219) | the user's `module_click` events (`docs/TRACKING.md`): 8 or more events, of any target, within 60 seconds | nightly at 02:00 UTC, over the module_click events of the previous UTC day | the time of the run (02:00:00 UTC); one row per user and day on which the rule fired |
    12	
    13	`velocity` was added against click fraud on the related-items module (scripts that click product cards in bursts).
    14	Its threshold was set on July 2026 related-items traffic, in which no human reached it.
